---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="SOCHSE is a founder-operated consulting and custom software practice led by Srijit."
  path="/about/"
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="About SOCHSE"
    title="Founder-led by design."
    description="SOCHSE is operated by Srijit as a consulting and custom software practice. Work stays deliberately scoped, practical, and close to the person responsible for delivery."
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="site-container grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[0.72fr_1.28fr]">
      <div>
        <span class="tag">Srijit · Founder</span>
      </div>
      <div class="prose max-w-3xl">
        <p class="text-xl leading-8 text-[var(--text)]">
          SOCHSE exists for problems that sit awkwardly between consulting,
          operations, data, and software.
        </p>
        <p>
          The working approach is simple: understand the real constraint, use
          an existing tool when it is sufficient, and build a narrow system
          only when doing so creates durable value.
        </p>
        <p>
          Founder work spans healthcare websites, private market-research
          systems, intelligence gathering, long-video processing, Android
          applications, on-device machine-learning exploration, and isolated
          client infrastructure.
        </p>

        <h2>The name</h2>
        <p>
          SOCHSE draws from <em>soch</em>—thought, thinking, or
          intelligence—and <em>se</em>, suggesting “with” or “through.” The
          idea is simple: work with thought. Understand the problem before
          choosing the tool.
        </p>

        <h2>How SOCHSE works</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Small, explicit outcomes before large commitments.</li>
          <li>Direct communication with the person doing the work.</li>
          <li>Client-owned data and infrastructure where practical.</li>
          <li>Reusable engineering without mixing client data.</li>
          <li>Honest boundaries around work in progress and private systems.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Capacity</h2>
        <p>
          SOCHSE is not presented as a large agency. Work is accepted
          selectively, scoped around available founder capacity, and may use
          explicitly identified specialists when a project genuinely needs
          them.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
